            <ArticleTitle>Soft tissue radiography in painful shoulder.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>393-400</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Specialized soft tissue radiography was applied to the shoulder region to differentiate between shoulder peritendinitis and radiating cervical pain. The technique is presented, together with the results of a clinical trial. Local inflammation was demonstrable even in the absence of calcific deposits.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
